    "body": "The 2027 BMW i3 and iX3 start at $61,500, but the electric sedan is nearly $80 less a month to lease.\nHow much does it cost to lease the 2027 BMW i3 and iX3?\nBMW opened orders for the 2027 i3 at the end of September, joining the new iX3 that went on sale earlier this year.\nThe i3 is essentially the sedan counterpart to the iX3 SUV, built on the same dedicated Neue Klasse EV platform with an 800V electrical system and BMW’s sixth-generation (Gen6) eDrive technology.\nBoth support DC fast charging of up to 400 kW, enabling them to charge from 10% to 80% in about 21 minutes. They also both have a standard NACS Charge port.\nAdvertisement - scroll for more content\nThe 2027 BMW i3 and iX3 use the same 108.7 kWh battery, offering ranges of up to 468 miles and 434 miles, respectively. With its taller, more upright SUV design, it’s no surprise the iX3 comes in a bit short of the i3 sedan.\n2027 BMW i3 50 xDrive interior (Source: BMW)\nInside, BMW’s newest EVs feature its Neue Klasse interior design. The setup includes BMW’s new Panoramic Vision, a full-length windshield display, and a 17.9″ central infotainment screen with its latest Operating System X. Buyers can upgrade to the optional BMW 3D Head-Up Display.\nThe 2027 BMW i3 50 xDrive and 2027 iX3 50 xDrive are now available to order, with prices starting at $61,500 for both.\nAccording to BMW’s payment estimator, the i3 is considerably more expensive to lease than its SUV counterpart.\nThe 2027 BMW i3 50 xDrive costs $784 a month according to the estimator. That’s for a 36-month lease with $4,999 due at signing. The 2027 BMW iX3 50 xDrive, on the other hand, costs $862 a month for the same 36-month lease with $4,999 due at signing.\nIf they are the same price, why is the i3 cheaper to lease? BMW’s estimated monthly payments include dealer contributions and other credits.\nThe 2027 i3 doesn’t have an advertised special lease cash or APR rates yet. However, the iX3 is available with a 4.99% APR for 60 months, which can be stacked with a $500 loyalty discount.\nSince the i3 just went on sale about two weeks ago, BMW will likely introduce new offers and incentives shortly, as it did with the iX3.\nBMW’s current offers end on November 2. Want to see what deals are available near you? We’ve made it easy with our partner link found below.\n2027 BMW iX3 — See offers near you\nFTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links. More.\nStay up to date with the latest content by subscribing to Electrek on Google News . You’re reading Electrek— experts who break news about Tesla , electric vehicles, and green energy , day after day. Be sure to check out our homepage for all the latest news, and follow Electrek on Twitter , Facebook , and LinkedIn to stay in the loop. Don’t know where to start? Check out our YouTube channel for the latest reviews.",
